    "description": "Vintage Vacuum Tube Lot - 7 Pieces\nAntique Radio and Audio Vacuum Tubes\nCollection of seven vintage vacuum tubes from the early era of radio and audio amplification. These classic glass tubes feature four-pin and five-pin base configurations common to early broadcast receivers and antique electronics.\nLot of 7 vintage glass vacuum tubes with 4-pin and 5-pin bases\nHytron branding visible on base; two tubes have tape marked 71A\nMix of clear glass envelopes and silvered getter flashing\nCondition:\nGlass envelopes intact without cracks. Bases show cosmetic wear, dust, and age patina. Pins exhibit light oxidation. Untested for functionality.\nAny electronic items or components have only been tested for power and are not eligible for returns based on functionality. All of our testing notes will be included in the listing details, if no notes are provided, item was unable to be tested.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
